      "side": 1,
      "message": "Q: This logic feels a bit strange:\nIf the driver doesn\u0027t provide a resume callback \u003d\u003e dev-\u003epowered \u003d 1 (So I imagine it is always powered on)\nIf the driver doesn\u0027t provide a suspend callback \u003d\u003e dev-\u003epowered \u003d 0\nWhy don\u0027t we modify the state of dev-\u003epowered in the suspend/resume callbacks ?",
      "revId": "f5b7aaefd01c4cb7854c4cd5b79eb65c6e921bed",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b36eebbb_fb0e0431",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
